---
// src/pages/share/freedom-vs-control/sources.astro
import Base from '../../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Nav from '../../../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../../../components/Footer.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Sources — Freedom vs. Control — Skovgard 2026"
  description="Primary sources and research notes supporting the Freedom vs. Control share message about Wyoming's 2025–2026 election legislation."
>
  <Nav />
  <main class="pt-20">

    <!-- Breadcrumb bar -->
    <div class="bg-wy-bone border-b border-gray-200 py-3 px-4">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto flex items-center gap-2 flex-wrap text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest">
        <a href="/share" class="text-gray-400 hover:text-wy-ember transition-colors">All messages</a>
        <span class="text-gray-300">/</span>
        <a href="/share/freedom-vs-control" class="text-gray-400 hover:text-wy-ember transition-colors">Freedom vs. Control</a>
        <span class="text-gray-300">/</span>
        <span class="text-wy-charcoal">Sources</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Header -->
    <div class="bg-wy-charcoal py-14 px-4 text-center">
      <p class="text-wy-sandstone font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-xs mb-3">Research Notes</p>
      <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-serif font-extrabold text-wy-bone mb-4 leading-tight">
        Freedom vs. Control
      </h1>
      <p class="text-wy-bone/70 text-lg max-w-xl mx-auto">
        Sources and research notes supporting the claims in the share message.
        This is a research aid, not a legal opinion.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Preamble -->
    <section class="bg-wy-bone border-b border-gray-200 py-10 px-4">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
        <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-xl px-6 py-5">
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
            <strong>About this page.</strong> This page documents the primary sources behind the
            Freedom vs. Control share message. The campaign reviewed Wyoming's 2025 General Session
            and 2026 Budget Session election bills — 38 flagged for review — and identified one
            access-positive item: 2025 SEA&nbsp;75&nbsp;/&nbsp;SF0165, which allows cancellation
            notices to be sent by email in addition to first-class mail. The major enacted legislation
            reviewed generally moved toward additional proof requirements, voter-list verification,
            limits on unsolicited absentee request forms, election-funding restrictions, or technical
            changes to voter qualifications. The 38-bill figure is a first-pass screening number, not
            a final legal determination.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Claims and support -->
    <article class="bg-wy-bone py-12 px-4">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto sources-content">

        <h2>Key claims and source support</h2>

        <div class="claims-table" role="table" aria-label="Claims and source support">
          <div class="claims-header" role="row">
            <span role="columnheader">Public statement</span>
            <span role="columnheader">Source support</span>
          </div>
          <div class="claims-row" role="row">
            <div role="cell">
              HB0156 requires proof of citizenship, proof of residence, and a 30-day residency rule.
            </div>
            <div role="cell">
              HB0156 enrolled act states it requires a qualified elector to be a bona fide Wyoming
              resident for at least 30 days before the election, requires documentation proving
              residence, prohibits registration based on documentation showing noncitizen status, and
              requires proof of United States citizenship and proof of residence on voter registration
              oath forms.
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="claims-row" role="row">
            <div role="cell">
              SF0078 restricts who may distribute unsolicited absentee ballot request forms.
            </div>
            <div role="cell">
              SF0078 enrolled act provides that no person, except for a county clerk, Secretary of
              State, or designee, shall distribute an absentee ballot request form to a voter unless
              the voter specifically solicits that form.
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="claims-row" role="row">
            <div role="cell">
              SF0030 is a voter-registration revisions bill tied to qualified-elector language.
            </div>
            <div role="cell">
              The 2026 Wyoming Legislature bill page identifies SF0030 as
              "Elections-voter registration revisions." Use the enrolled act for exact statutory
              language when quoting.
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="claims-row" role="row">
            <div role="cell">
              SEA&nbsp;75&nbsp;/&nbsp;SF0165 adds email notice in addition to mail for voter
              registration cancellations.
            </div>
            <div role="cell">
              The Wyoming Secretary of State's 2025 election legislation page identifies
              Ch.166&nbsp;/&nbsp;SF0165&nbsp;/&nbsp;SEA75 as "Cancellation of Registration Notice —
              Amendments." Review the enrolled act for exact notice text.
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="claims-row" role="row">
            <div role="cell">
              The 38-bill figure is a first-pass screening count.
            </div>
            <div role="cell">
              This figure comes from a Step 1 screening that flagged bills touching voting,
              registration, ballot access, absentee voting, voter rolls, election administration, or
              candidate access. It should be described as "flagged for review," not as a final court
              finding or exhaustive count.
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <h2>Primary sources</h2>

        <div class="source-list">

          <div class="source-item">
            <p class="source-label">
              HB0156, 2025 — House Enrolled Act 57
              <span class="source-desc">Proof of voter residency and registration qualifications</span>
            </p>
            <a href="https://www.wyoleg.gov/2025/Enroll/HB0156.pdf"
               target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="source-link">
              wyoleg.gov/2025/Enroll/HB0156.pdf
            </a>
            <p class="source-note">
              Use for exact language on proof of citizenship, proof of residence, and 30-day residency.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="source-item">
            <p class="source-label">
              SF0078, 2025 — Senate Enrolled Act 10
              <span class="source-desc">Prohibition on distribution of unsolicited ballot request forms</span>
            </p>
            <a href="https://www.wyoleg.gov/2025/Enroll/SF0078.pdf"
               target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="source-link">
              wyoleg.gov/2025/Enroll/SF0078.pdf
            </a>
            <p class="source-note">
              Use for exact language on unsolicited absentee ballot request forms.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="source-item">
            <p class="source-label">
              SF0030, 2026
              <span class="source-desc">Elections — voter registration revisions</span>
            </p>
            <a href="https://wyoleg.gov/Legislation/2026/SF0030"
               target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="source-link">
              wyoleg.gov/Legislation/2026/SF0030
            </a>
            <p class="source-note">
              Use the bill page and enrolled act for exact current-law language.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="source-item">
            <p class="source-label">
              SF0165&nbsp;/&nbsp;SEA75&nbsp;/&nbsp;Ch.166, 2025
              <span class="source-desc">Cancellation of registration notice — amendments</span>
            </p>
            <a href="https://sos.wyo.gov/Elections/Legislation/2025/Chp166_SF165_SEA75_Cancellation-of-Registration-Notice-Amendments.pdf"
               target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="source-link">
              sos.wyo.gov — Ch.166 / SF0165 / SEA75 (PDF)
            </a>
            <p class="source-note">
              Wyoming Secretary of State publication. Use for the email-notice provision associated
              with voter registration cancellation notices.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="source-item">
            <p class="source-label">
              HB0318, 2025 — House Enrolled Act 62
              <span class="source-desc">Maintenance of voter lists</span>
            </p>
            <a href="https://www.wyoleg.gov/2025/Enroll/HB0318.pdf"
               target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="source-link">
              wyoleg.gov/2025/Enroll/HB0318.pdf
            </a>
            <p class="source-note">
              Use for voter-list maintenance, data matching, and registration cancellation review.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="source-item">
            <p class="source-label">
              HB0228, 2025 — House Enrolled Act 65
              <span class="source-desc">Prohibition on private funds for conducting elections</span>
            </p>
            <a href="https://www.wyoleg.gov/2025/Enroll/HB0228.pdf"
               target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="source-link">
              wyoleg.gov/2025/Enroll/HB0228.pdf
            </a>
            <p class="source-note">
              Use for election funding, voter education, voter outreach, and voter-registration
              program language.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="source-item">
            <p class="source-label">
              Wyoming Constitution — Secretary of State publication
            </p>
            <a href="https://sos.wyo.gov/Forms/Publications/WYConstitution.pdf"
               target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="source-link">
              sos.wyo.gov — Wyoming Constitution (PDF)
            </a>
            <p class="source-note">
              Use for Article 1, Section 27 (elections free and equal) and related constitutional provisions.
            </p>
          </div>

        </div>

        <h2>Public-safe wording</h2>

        <blockquote class="safe-wording">
          Based on the official bill text reviewed, HB0156 appears to raise the clearest voter-access
          and constitutional concern because it requires proof of citizenship, proof of residence, and
          a 30-day Wyoming residency rule before voter eligibility. Across the 2025 and 2026 review,
          the major election bills identified did far more to tighten registration, verification,
          absentee-ballot procedures, voter-list maintenance, election funding, or ballot access than
          to expand voter access.
        </blockquote>

        <h2>Notes for responsible use</h2>

        <ul class="responsible-list">
          <li>Use "appears to," "may restrict," and "first-pass review" when discussing bills that require legal interpretation or implementation facts not yet settled.</li>
          <li>Use enrolled acts for claims about laws that passed. Do not quote from bill versions that did not become law.</li>
          <li>Use bill pages, legislative journals, and roll-call votes for claims about who voted for a bill.</li>
          <li>Treat failed bills as evidence of legislative direction or future risk, not as current law.</li>
          <li>Separate voter-access claims from election-administration claims. Not all election bills restrict voter access.</li>
        </ul>

      </div>
    </article>

    <!-- Back CTA -->
    <div class="bg-white py-12 px-4 border-t border-gray-200 text-center">
      <a href="/share/freedom-vs-control"
         class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-6 py-3 bg-wy-ember text-wy-bone font-bold rounded-lg hover:bg-wy-ember-dark transition-colors text-sm">
        <svg class="w-4 h-4 shrink-0" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M15 19l-7-7 7-7" />
        </svg>
        Back to Freedom vs. Control
      </a>
    </div>

  </main>
  <Footer />
</Base>

<style>
  /* Sources content typography */
  .sources-content { line-height: 1.75; color: #2b2b2b; }
  .sources-content h2 {
    font-family: 'Bitter', serif;
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 1.375rem;
    color: #2b2b2b;
    margin: 2.5rem 0 1rem;
    padding-bottom: 0.5rem;
    border-bottom: 2px solid #c68a4a;
  }
  .sources-content h2:first-child { margin-top: 0; }

  /* Claims support table */
  .claims-table {
    border: 1px solid #ddd8ce;
    border-radius: 10px;
    overflow: hidden;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }
  .claims-header {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 2fr 3fr;
    background: #2b2b2b;
    gap: 0;
  }
  .claims-header span {
    padding: 10px 16px;
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    color: #f1ece1;
  }
  .claims-header span:first-child {
    border-right: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.12);
  }
  .claims-row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 2fr 3fr;
    border-bottom: 1px solid #ddd8ce;
  }
  .claims-row:last-child { border-bottom: none; }
  .claims-row div {
    padding: 14px 16px;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: #2b2b2b;
  }
  .claims-row div:first-child {
    background: #f1ece1;
    border-right: 1px solid #ddd8ce;
    font-weight: 500;
  }
  .claims-row div:last-child { background: #fafaf8; }
  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .claims-header { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .claims-header span:first-child { border-right: none; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.12); }
    .claims-row { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .claims-row div:first-child { border-right: none; border-bottom: 1px solid #ddd8ce; }
  }

  /* Source list */
  .source-list {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1px;
    border: 1px solid #e5e2da;
    border-radius: 10px;
    overflow: hidden;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }
  .source-item {
    background: #fff;
    padding: 16px 20px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid #e5e2da;
  }
  .source-item:last-child { border-bottom: none; }
  .source-label {
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    color: #0f2742;
    margin: 0 0 4px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1px;
  }
  .source-desc {
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    color: #6b7280;
  }
  .source-link {
    display: inline-block;
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    color: #b22234;
    text-decoration: none;
    word-break: break-all;
    margin-bottom: 4px;
  }
  .source-link:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
  .source-note {
    margin: 4px 0 0;
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    color: #6b7280;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  /* Public-safe wording */
  .safe-wording {
    background: #fefce8;
    border-left: 4px solid #c68a4a;
    border-radius: 0 8px 8px 0;
    padding: 16px 20px;
    margin: 0 0 2rem;
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: #2b2b2b;
    font-style: normal;
  }

  /* Responsible use list */
  .responsible-list {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 10px;
  }
  .responsible-list li {
    display: flex;
    gap: 10px;
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    color: #374151;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  .responsible-list li::before {
    content: "•";
    color: #c68a4a;
    font-weight: 700;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    margin-top: 2px;
  }
</style>
